[{:adr/authoritative_for ["cloud-itonami-isic-5820 Lead + Contact entity addition" "lead-status-gate / lead-convertible-gate governor checks"], :adr/topic "isic-5820-lead-contact-entities", :adr/related ["adr-2607173300" "adr-2607172600" "adr-2607173100"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607173400-isic-5820-lead-contact-entities", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-18", :adr/body "# ADR-2607173400: cloud-itonami-isic-5820 -- Lead + Contact entities with governed qualify/convert flow\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-18\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner directive: \\\"\u6280\u8853\u7a74\u57cb\u3081\\\" -- selecting the technical-gap-filling path out of ADR-2607173300's coverage assessment, over lead-acquisition-first)\n**Scope**: `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5820` (child commit `3ec555f5c102`), west pin advance.\n**Builds on**: ADR-2607173300 (coverage assessment identified: no Contact, no Lead, no Task/Activity, no custom-field mechanism -- \\\"NO field anywhere in this schema for marketing-campaign attribution\\\").\n\n## Decision\n\nClosed the single biggest data-model gap from the coverage assessment: added **Lead** and **Contact** as first-class entities, governed by two new SubscriptionGovernor hard gates, reusing the shared `kotoba.crm.pipeline` ordered-stage validator for a SECOND domain (lead-qualification lifecycle, not just opportunity stages -- that library's own docstring names \\\"marketing lifecycle stages\\\" as an intended reuse target, confirming this was the designed extension point, not scope creep).\n\n- **Entities**: Lead `{id name email company source status account-id owner-rep-id}`, Contact `{id account-id lead-id name email role}`. Full `Store` protocol extension across all three backends (MemStore, DatomicStore with new schema/tx/pull fns, FileStore which delegates + persists per its existing wrapper pattern).\n- **Lead lifecycle**: `lead-status-order [:new :working :qualified]` + `lead-exit-statuses #{:disqualified}`, validated via `kotoba.crm.pipeline/valid-transition?` (same no-skip discipline as the opportunity pipeline). `:lead/qualify` op advances status, follows the same phase 0-3 progression as opportunity transitions (auto-commits at phase 3 when governor-clean).\n- **Conversion**: `:lead/convert` mints a real Contact + Opportunity from a qualified lead. Gated by `lead-convertible-gate`: the lead must be exactly `:qualified` AND already account-matched (`:account-id` set) -- the LLM proposes the draft, the governor alone decides readiness, same philosophy as every other hard gate in this actor. **Deliberately never in any phase's `:auto` set** (same treatment as `:dispute/request`) -- minting new records is a bigger, less-reversible action than a routine status advance, so it stays approval-gated even at the most permissive phase.\n- Account creation-on-convert was explicitly NOT built (a lead converts only against an already-existing/matched account) -- consistent with this actor's \\\"honest scope\\\" discipline; flagged as a documented future extension, not silently glossed over.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Full test suite: 77 tests / 274 assertions, 0 failures (was 63/200 before this change). clj-kondo: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `dev/real_advisor_check.clj` extended and re-run live against `murakumo-main` (qwen3.6, ADR-2607173100): both `:lead/qualify` and `:lead/convert` returned well-formed, correctly-typed EDN proposals from the real model, routed through the same actor graph as every other op.\n- New tests cover: read/write parity across both store backends, the lead-status-gate's skip-rejection, the lead-convertible-gate's not-yet-qualified rejection AND missing-account-id rejection, the full escalate-then-approve-then-commit path for conversion, and file-store persistence round-trip for a converted lead's minted Contact/Opportunity.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- The store can now represent a real top-of-funnel lead, not just accounts/opportunities that already exist -- a precondition for using this actor as an operational (not merely architectural-proof) sales tool.\n- Follow-up (not done here): account-creation-on-convert, an HTTP endpoint surfacing leads (current HTTP layer has no per-entity read endpoints for ANY entity, by existing minimal-surface design -- adding one is a separate decision), persistent/production deployment (tracked separately).\n", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-18", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607173400: cloud-itonami-isic-5820 Lead + Contact entities with governed qualify/convert flow", :adr/source-format "edn"}]